From: pmOS Q706F fixes
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: drop gadget pullup on USB_ROLE_NONE

TCPM reports cable detach as USB_ROLE_NONE. If the controller is already
in device mode, dwc3_set_mode() does not change the port and the
gadget keeps D+ pulled up, so usb0 stays configured after the
Type-C partner is gone. Disconnect on none and connect again when
the port returns to device.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
@@ -469,6 +469,21 @@
 	}
 
 	dwc3_pre_set_role(dwc, role);
+
+	/*
+	 * Cable detach is USB_ROLE_NONE while the port is already in
+	 * device mode. dwc3_set_mode() then no-ops, so an enumerated
+	 * gadget keeps D+ pulled up and usb0 stays configured with no
+	 * Type-C partner. Drop the pullup until the next device role.
+	 */
+	if (role == USB_ROLE_NONE) {
+		if (dwc->gadget)
+			usb_gadget_disconnect(dwc->gadget);
+	} else if (role == USB_ROLE_DEVICE) {
+		if (dwc->gadget)
+			usb_gadget_connect(dwc->gadget);
+	}
+
 	dwc3_set_mode(dwc, mode);
 	return 0;
 }
